bol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/generatedcacertificate","title":"GeneratedCaCertificate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Response returned when a CA certificate is generated. Includes the private key PEM, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"once"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and never stored or retrievable again — when the custodian produced one at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all. Under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vault_pki"},{"type":"text","text":" custody the key was born inside Vault and there is nothing to return,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the point of that custodian rather than a shortcoming of this response."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/GeneratedCaCertificate/mtlsTrustAnchor":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this CA is offered as a trust anchor for mutual TLS. When set, the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports this CA’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"public"}]},{"type":"text","text":" certificate to the bundle named by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AXIAM__SERVER__TLS__CLIENT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH"},{"type":"text","text":" at startup and turns client-certificate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authentication on ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optional"},{"type":"text","text":") if the operator has not configured it explicitly. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client presenting a certificate that chains to this CA is then verified by the TLS layer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"itself, which is what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam_pki::mtls"},{"type":"text","text":" needs to authenticate an IoT device or a service"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account by certificate rather than by secret. # What is and is not copied Only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public_cert_pem"},{"type":"text","text":" — the certificate. The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"private key stays where its custodian put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Vault, or sealed into the row) and is never written to the server volume. A trust"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anchor is public by construction: it is what the server hands every client during the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TLS handshake, and every device that has to validate the chain already holds a copy. #"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Why a restart rustls builds its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootCertStore"},{"type":"text","text":" once, when the listener is constructed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and actix-web binds that config for the process’s life. Toggling this changes what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"next"}]},{"type":"text","text":" boot trusts, and the API says so in its response rather than pretending the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change took effect. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", so a deployment that never touches this keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly the TLS posture it has today."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mtlsTrustAnchor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/generatedcacertificate\/mtlstrustanchor","title":"mtlsTrustAnchor","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/GeneratedCaCertificate\/mtlsTrustAnchor"},"doc://AxiamSDK/